35,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"It seems that moving our connections comes with a cost for every change, and we are paying for space we aren't even using. I believe we should be very mindful of this as we plan.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The staff survey shows a strong preference for daylight, yet the current plan leaves several people against the wall. We must be honest about the fact that some seats are objectively worse than others.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"Um... I found out that we're billed by area, not people. Even empty desks cost us about 41,000 yen a month. I'm... I'm a bit worried about how that affects our budget.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Wow, 41,000 yen for an empty desk?! That's crazy! Also, I found out that setting up screens and power takes up to nine minutes every morning. That's a lot of time wasted when we're already so busy!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"It's fascinating how we're obsessing over minutes and yen while ignoring the actual experience of sitting. The printer area is a noise trap, and our gear takes days of tweaking to actually fit a human body.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"It is a bit surprising, isn't it? Since each change to our layout costs us more, I think it would be wonderful if we could find a plan we all truly love the first time.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Shizue, finding a plan everyone ""loves"" is unrealistic when the layout creates a hierarchy of quality. If we ignore who gets the window and who is stuck against the wall, we are just delaying a conflict.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,Um... I agree with Toshio-san that it's difficult. But... I also found that the new joiners learned a lot just by overhearing us. Maybe we should think about how we sit to help each other?,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Daisuke, that's a great point! But we also have to think about the time! If we have to spend nearly ten minutes every morning just getting set up, it's going to eat into our focus time.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Mio, ten minutes is a rounding error in a workday. What's not a rounding error is the chronic back pain from a poorly adjusted chair or the distraction of a printer humming in your ear for eight hours. Let's prioritize ergonomics over ""setup time.""","{""words"":44,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shizue,,It is a bit sad to hear that some of you are in pain or feeling distracted. Perhaps we can find a balance where we support each other's well-being while being mindful of the costs.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Shizue, balance is a vague term. We have a limited number of window seats and a high cost for changes. We need to decide now who takes the less desirable spots to avoid future resentment.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"Um... I don't want anyone to feel resentful. Maybe if we arrange the desks so we can still overhear each other, like the new joiners did, the ""worse"" seats won't feel so isolating?","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Shunichi, it's not just a rounding error when you have meetings back-to-back! Those little gaps are precious. If we can find a way to avoid that daily setup struggle, we'll all be much happier and more focused!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Mio, your ""precious gaps"" are just a lack of time management. I'm talking about the physical toll of the environment. If we ignore the noise and ergonomics, we're just optimizing the speed at which we burn out.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"It seems we all have very different things weighing on our hearts. Let us remember that we are a team; if we listen to each other with kindness, I am sure we can find a way.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Toshio,,Kindness does not change the physical layout of the room. We have a clear conflict between the number of window seats and the number of people. Let us be pragmatic and decide the allocation criteria now.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"Um... I just don't want us to fight. If we can find a layout that helps the new people learn and keeps the costs down, maybe we can all agree on it together?","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Mio,,"@Toshio, being pragmatic is good, but we can't forget the daily grind! If we pick a layout that's a pain to set up every morning, we're just adding stress to everyone's day. Let's find a way to make it easy!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Toshio, for once, I agree. Pragmatism is the only way out of this. Let's stop talking about ""feelings"" and ""gaps"" and actually look at the options. I'll be voting for whatever minimizes the noise and maximizes stability.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Daisuke,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,Mio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
