58,3,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
59,3,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"It is a pleasure to see our options. I worry that Option A might make us feel a bit adrift, and Option C seems like it would be very expensive with all those changes. What do you all think?","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Toshio,,Option A is the most honest solution. It acknowledges that some seats are better than others and ensures no one is permanently relegated to the wall. It removes the hierarchy and the potential for resentment.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"Um... I'm worried about Option A too. If we move every day, will the new joiners still be able to overhear us and learn? And... wouldn't clearing the desks every day be a lot of work?","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Mio,,"@Daisuke, exactly! Option A is a nightmare! I found out that setting up takes up to nine minutes every morning. Doing that every single day would eat up all our breaks! I'm definitely against it!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Mio, for once, your obsession with minutes is actually useful. Option A is a disaster; spending days tweaking a chair only to lose the setting by tomorrow is absurd. I'm voting for Option B. Stability is the only rational choice.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Shunichi, I agree that stability is a comfort. Option B would allow us to settle in and truly get to know those sitting beside us, without the worry of constant costs or daily setup.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Shizue, stability is only a comfort for those who get the window seats. Option B simply freezes the inequality in place. If we choose B, we must explicitly decide who takes the worst seats now.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"Um... I don't like the idea of deciding who gets the ""worst"" seat. But if we choose Option C, wouldn't the cost of moving everyone be really high? I'm... I'm leaning toward Option B, if we can be fair.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Toshio, we can just rotate the window seats manually every few months if we have to! But Option C sounds like a huge hassle for everyone. Option B is way better because we can just sit down and start working!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Toshio, your obsession with ""inequality"" is exhausting. A window is a luxury, not a human right. I'd rather be ""unequal"" in a chair that actually fits my back than ""equal"" in a state of constant physical discomfort. Option B.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"It is heartening to see us finding common ground. If we choose Option B, we can carefully decide our neighbors together, ensuring everyone feels included and supported without the burden of extra costs.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Shizue, ""carefully deciding"" is just a polite way of avoiding the conflict. If we choose Option B, we are assigning a permanent disadvantage to some. I cannot support a plan that ignores this reality.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"Um... @Toshio-san, maybe we could just... talk about it? If we choose Option B, we can try to be kind and make sure no one feels left out. I think it's better than the other options.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Mio,,"@Toshio, please! We can just be nice about it! Option B is the only one that doesn't waste our time every single morning. Let's just pick B and figure out the seats together!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Toshio, your commitment to ""fairness"" is becoming a hindrance to actual productivity. We've already established that the physical cost of instability is too high. Let's stop the philosophy lesson and just vote for Option B.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Shizue,,It seems we have reached a gentle consensus. Option B allows us to cherish our connections and our health without unnecessary costs. I will cast my vote for Option B.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"I cannot support a system that masks inequality with politeness. However, since the majority prioritizes stability over fairness, I will vote for Option A to remain consistent in my stance against permanent hierarchy.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,"Um... I'm still a bit worried about the budget and the new joiners, but I think Option B is the safest choice for everyone's peace of mind. I'll vote for Option B.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Mio,,I'm so glad we're on the same page! No more wasting our precious morning gaps on plugging in screens! I'm voting for Option B!,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,Finally. I'm voting for Option B. Let's prioritize a functional workspace over a social experiment in equality. I'll be the one ensuring my desk is far from the printer.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
